Others have already pointed out that the mechanics are Ricoh, thank
you.

Not mentioned so far afaict: multiple LN03 family members, toner
safety precautions.

There were multiple flavours of LN03, can't remember many details, but
the differences are likely things like "does it do PostScript" rather
than anything more fundamental.

If you are tempted to clean out the inside, think first. Toner is
unpleasant stuff, and potentially gets everywhere. The filters in
ordinary vacuum cleaners typically don't catch toner, so it comes
straight out again out of the other side of the cleaner. There used to
be (afaict still are) specific vacuum cleaners around intended for use
by photocopier engineers etc (and what is a laserprinter but a
photocopier without the optical input).

hth
