There are, as far as I remember, two versions of the LN03. Called LN03 
and LN03-Plus. The -Plus have more memory, but I don't think it differs 
in any other way.

There was also a Postscript printer produced by DEC, using the same 
mechanics. But that printer don't wear the label "LN03", but instead 
says "Scriptprinter".
Totally different firmware, but all the mechanical parts are 
interchangeable. The Scriptprinter cannot take any cartridges, by the 
way. Those two holes are blocked.

