Wrt benchmarks: if low level stuff is your thing (not everyone can
afford a TPC-class setup, or even a SPECwhatever setup), there's
surely still McCalpin streams for memory bandwidth, and more recently
there's CoreMark, which is nominally targetted at the embedded world,
but nothing to stop anyone getting the source, and running it on an
IA64 or AMD64 or ARM11 or whatever. If you ask Coremark for Intel
scores the results include the usual x86-family stuff but also one
Itanium result. A colleague tells me the suite is fairly compact, so
if someone were so inclined they could in principle do VAX and Alpha
benchmarks, for historical interest.

